IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. F02-SAFE-SEQ-READ.
*> Safe sequential read loop using FILE STATUS (00 and 10).
*> Prevents reading past EOF (status 46) or stale buffer reads.

ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
FILE-CONTROL.
    SELECT CDR-FILE ASSIGN TO "cdr_input.dat"
        ORGANIZATION IS LINE SEQUENTIAL
        FILE STATUS IS WS-CDR-STATUS.

DATA DIVISION.
FILE SECTION.
FD  CDR-FILE.
01  CDR-REC             PIC X(80).

WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01  WS-CDR-STATUS       PIC X(2) VALUE SPACES.
    88  CDR-OK          VALUE "00".
    88  CDR-EOF         VALUE "10".
01  WS-EOF-FLAG         PIC X(1) VALUE "N".
    88  EOF-REACHED     VALUE "Y".
01  WS-CDR-WORK         PIC X(80).
01  WS-REC-COUNT        PIC 9(7) VALUE 0.

PROCEDURE DIVISION.
0000-MAIN.
    OPEN INPUT CDR-FILE
    IF NOT CDR-OK
        DISPLAY "OPEN FAILED: " WS-CDR-STATUS
        MOVE 16 TO RETURN-CODE
        STOP RUN
    END-IF

    PERFORM UNTIL EOF-REACHED
        READ CDR-FILE INTO WS-CDR-WORK
        EVALUATE TRUE
            WHEN CDR-OK
                ADD 1 TO WS-REC-COUNT
            WHEN CDR-EOF
                SET EOF-REACHED TO TRUE
            WHEN OTHER
                DISPLAY "READ ERROR: " WS-CDR-STATUS
                SET EOF-REACHED TO TRUE
        END-EVALUATE
    END-PERFORM

    CLOSE CDR-FILE
    DISPLAY "RECORDS PROCESSED: " WS-REC-COUNT
    STOP RUN.
